{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299882-what-if-someone-else-won-the-ascension-war","id":1299882,"title":"What if someone else won the Ascension war?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-26T01:24:56-07:00","id":1299882,"title":"What if someone else won the Ascension war?","content":"So the order of reason won the ascension war, and imposed their paradigm on the Masses. <br /> <br /> What happens if someone else had won? <br /> <br /> My tax:<br /> <br /> If the Celestial Chorus had won, they would have basically, well, imposed praying on everyone. Everyone would pray. The cities would be filled with chapels, sanctuaries, and all sorts of religious buildings. Those with Awakened powers, would be called 'saints' or 'blessed by god'. You would have to be able to properly understand and accept The One, to hear his song, to be able to ascend to the higher ranks. Those who go against the Celestial Chorus, whether by insufficient piety or outright using of other paradigms, are to be considered 'heretics', 'deviants', 'apostates', and are to be hunted down without mercy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T01:58:08-07:00","id":1299888,"title":"","content":"The Messianic Voices Did Win. The Fellowship as much became the Cabal of Pure thought as the Celestial Chorus. As we've seen the vast changes from the Conventions of the Order of Reason to the Modern Technocracy It could have just as readily maintained its Christian Elements without accepting Enlightement Humanism. Why the Order of Reason ultimately drops Religion is Religion allows a place for &quot;Outsiders' and the Technocracy wants one world, one belief.<br /> <br /> A celestial world has a place for the &quot;infernal&quot; for the &quot;wicked&quot; and.. may in fact give far too much power to such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T04:34:17-07:00","id":1299903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299882-what-if-someone-else-won-the-ascension-war#post1299882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the order of reason won the ascension war, and imposed their paradigm on the Masses.<br /> <br /> What happens if someone else had won?<br /> <br /> My tax:<br /> <br /> If the Celestial Chorus had won, they would have basically, well, imposed praying on everyone. Everyone would pray. The cities would be filled with chapels, sanctuaries, and all sorts of religious buildings. Those with Awakened powers, would be called 'saints' or 'blessed by god'. You would have to be able to properly understand and accept The One, to hear his song, to be able to ascend to the higher ranks. Those who go against the Celestial Chorus, whether by insufficient piety or outright using of other paradigms, are to be considered 'heretics', 'deviants', 'apostates', and are to be hunted down without mercy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This one is tricky. The Celestial Chorus is very specifically the monotheistic group that embraces differences. You're already on the right track by not limiting them to Christianity, but I think the hunting people down without mercy misses the mark. Assuming that an ascendant Celestial Chorus would go tyrannical, they they would likely hunt people down <i>out of</i> mercy. Apostasy would be seen not as rebellion but as unfortunate defect. Those that could not hear the One would be lovingly collected and altered so that they could share in the experience of that great voice. It would be very much like forcibly rounding up the deaf and giving them hearing without asking; good intentions or not it would still be violation and tyranny.<br /> <br /> Again, that's assuming that an ascendant Celestial Chorus would go the totalitarian route. There are other ways a group can fall.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T05:22:14-07:00","id":1299912,"title":"","content":"What other ways?<br /> <br /> Also... If they hunt you down and forcibly brainwash you, not much mercy is seen. No matter what they say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T05:37:36-07:00","id":1299921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299882-what-if-someone-else-won-the-ascension-war?p=1299912#post1299912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What other ways?<br /> <br /> Also... If they hunt you down and forcibly brainwash you, not much mercy is seen. No matter what they say.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on who is doing the seeing, doesn't it? The recipients may not see the mercy, but then that is part of the problem with them. The tyrants certainly see that they are delivering mercy. <br /> <br /> Note: I am very much not trying to argue that the tyrants are doing a good thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>C S Lewis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201cOf all the tyrannies, a tyranny sincerely exercised for the good of its victims may be the most oppressive. It may be better to live under robber barons than under the omnipotent moral busybodies. The robber barons cruelty may sometimes sleep, his cupidity may at some point be satiated; but those who torment us for our own good will torment us without end, for they do so with the approval of their own conscience.\u201d</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> As for other ways that a group can fall... The Traditions vs Technocracy battle is very much a freedom vs security dynamic, but other struggles such as individualism vs communalism, fate vs free will, and humanism vs relativism are also possible. The Celestial Chorus Ascendant could just be a problem because it considers the world a place to surpass beyond and so lets it fall into decline. It might create a hell on earth simply by teaching that earth and the suffering on it are unimportant.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T05:38:37-07:00","id":1299923,"title":"","content":"How about verbena?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T06:24:02-07:00","id":1299937,"title":"","content":"Verbena had the Ascencion War won in their time, those Old Times where the Old Faith forged weapons in dragon's fire. If you want to see Verbena ascendant (and, perhaps, tyranical) one hasn't to look further than the ancient empires. Aztecs would be a very good model, but even Romans (with their Hermetic influence) are the kind of civilization that can be built upon the old faiths.<br /> <br /> A world where they control the Consensus it's a world filled with gods, supernatural creatures and magical bloodlines. Dragons, unicorns and the rest of bygones exist and thrive, Verbena wouldn't have it other way: Industrial revolution &quot;human power over the nature&quot; philosophies wouldn't be very accepted. I imagine humanity would have less predominance under such a world.<br /> <br /> Technology would be developed anyway (pre-christian civilizations had technology, sometimes better than what christians had) but it's develop would be slowed down, and it would be very influenced by this &quot;world of gods and monsters&quot; mentality. No important building would be made w/o the proper sacrifices. Politicians would claim to descend from a magical bloodline or another. Empires would claim their gods are the best gods...<br /> <br /> There's little need for a &quot;Masquerade&quot; as we understand it under such world-view, more likely people would make pacts with some supernatural beings to get protection against other kinds of supernatural beings. If vampires end up hiding as consecuence of understandable persecution (they ARE a plague, and Verbena don't like them 'cause they're undead), it would be as other kind of creature or being (now blood cults are a boon to the Masquerade rather than a breach).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-26-2019, 09:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T08:08:51-07:00","id":1299959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299882-what-if-someone-else-won-the-ascension-war?p=1299937#post1299937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Verbena had the Ascencion War won in their time, those Old Times where the Old Faith forged weapons in dragon's fire. If you want to see Verbena ascendant (and, perhaps, tyranical) one hasn't to look further than the ancient empires. Aztecs would be a very good model, but even Romans (with their Hermetic influence) are the kind of civilization that can be built upon the old faiths.<br /> <br /> A world where they control the Consensus it's a world filled with gods, supernatural creatures and magical bloodlines. Dragons, unicorns and the rest of bygones exist and thrive, Verbena wouldn't have it other way: Industrial revolution &quot;human power over the nature&quot; philosophies wouldn't be very accepted. I imagine humanity would have less predominance under such a world.<br /> <br /> Technology would be developed anyway (pre-christian civilizations had technology, sometimes better than what christians had) but it's develop would be slowed down, and it would be very influenced by this &quot;world of gods and monsters&quot; mentality. No important building would be made w/o the proper sacrifices. Politicians would claim to descend from a magical bloodline or another. Empires would claim their gods are the best gods...<br /> <br /> There's little need for a &quot;Masquerade&quot; as we understand it under such world-view, more likely people would make pacts with some supernatural beings to get protection against other kinds of supernatural beings. If vampires end up hiding as consecuence of understandable persecution (they ARE a plague, and Verbena don't like them 'cause they're undead), it would be as other kind of creature or being (now blood cults are a boon to the Masquerade rather than a breach).</div> </div> </div> </div>In other words... <br /> <br /> It was basically like Sword and Sorcery Conan the Barbarian?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T08:26:46-07:00","id":1299964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299882-what-if-someone-else-won-the-ascension-war?p=1299959#post1299959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was basically like Sword and Sorcery Conan the Barbarian?</div> </div> </div> </div>XD, perhaps. Verbena feed from the myths and fantasy that inspired Conan...they would want such feats and stories to be feasible.<br /> <br /> But remember that, as much as they want, the Technocracy can't use all their StarTrek+ level technology. If the Verbena were in their place, they shouldn't be able to pull all the epic fantasy shit they would want, nor entirely avoid a rise of technology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T08:43:41-07:00","id":1299970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299882-what-if-someone-else-won-the-ascension-war?p=1299964#post1299964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> XD, perhaps. Verbena feed from the myths and fantasy that inspired Conan...they would want such feats and stories to be feasible.<br /> <br /> But remember that, as much as they want, the Technocracy can't use all their StarTrek+ level technology. If the Verbena were in their place, they shouldn't be able to pull all the epic fantasy shit they would want, nor entirely avoid a rise of technology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Woah. <br /> <br /> So basically, in a far off world, where the Verbena won, it would be a place where law is weak, where wild beasts and monsters stalk in the wilds between villages. Where lone heroes with mighty thews, go against monsters of vast size and shape, in desolate ruins of steel, concrete, and glass?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T09:03:54-07:00","id":1299975,"title":"","content":"The Verbena are most connected to the ritual and calendar based magic of (usually polytheistic) agrarian societies. They are the ones who stand apart from or on the edges of regular society and do the hard things it takes to keep that society alive. They keep track of the great alignments to determine the best time to plant or the destiny of children. They treat with, defeat, or appease capricious gods to bring in the harvest or drive away disease. They serve out justice, bloody or otherwise, seen or otherwise, to keep that society in balance.<br /> <br /> A society crafted by the Verbena would be one that was very structured, but not in regular, predictable ways. Less the work 5 days and take 2 off, more auguries to determine if the day was auspicious or not (that was the way the Romans determined days off, by the way). Less living by the clock, more living by the sign. Religion would be important, based on sacrifice and schedule, and largely left to the experts. The things that go bump in the night would be dealt with not by destruction but by tacit agreement and mythic binding (&quot;you may prey on those foolish enough to enter the dark woods, but there will be no mercy for you if you step outside.&quot;)<br /> <br /> And if you are looking to see how the Verbena could fall, look at their role. They could leave their role as facilitators, diviners, and intercessors and just pursue their own power, leaving the world to burn. They could move from serving society by appeasing the gods to serving the old gods at the expense of society. Or they could decide that instead of being the power behind society, they should rule and then use their secret knowledge and their favors to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T09:55:47-07:00","id":1299984,"title":"","content":"The Wu Lung actually Won for awhile. You had to get a liscence from them to practice magic or got paradox. That's something even the Technocracy has never repeated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T10:05:07-07:00","id":1299986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299882-what-if-someone-else-won-the-ascension-war?p=1299984#post1299984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Wu Lung actually Won for awhile. You had to get a liscence from them to practice magic or got paradox. That's something even the Technocracy has never repeated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooh.... tell me more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T10:12:34-07:00","id":1299990,"title":"","content":"The victory of any faction would be unpleasant, as they would impose their flaws on the world and call them virtues. A world run by the Verbena would look a lot like the bloodiest parts of European history; Vikings, wickerman burning druids, and so forth. An unpleasant place to be if you were not one of the elite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T10:45:11-07:00","id":1299999,"title":"","content":"What about the DreamSpeakers? Or Hermetics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T11:41:30-07:00","id":1300018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299882-what-if-someone-else-won-the-ascension-war?p=1299999#post1299999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the DreamSpeakers? Or Hermetics?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Dreamspeaker victory would look like the cultures and nations of native people around the world, before conquest and destruction. A Hermetic victory would look like They of Forgotten Realms, or possibly the monks of Leng.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T12:14:12-07:00","id":1300028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299882-what-if-someone-else-won-the-ascension-war?p=1299999#post1299999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the DreamSpeakers? Or Hermetics?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A Dreamspeaker victory would be very strange because the Dreamspeakers aren't really a unified Tradition. Even according to Mage History they were pretty much a catch all for anyone who looked vaguely shamanistic. The idea that they would ever have come together as a group in a way that could take over the world is a stretch (not because they are incapable, but because without an outside threat there isn't much reason for many of them to even like each other). The idea that if they did they could agree on how to run it beggars belief. At best you'd see a sort of taking over the world and deliberately leaving it the hell alone.<br /> <br /> At least one of the factions that started the Order of Reason was a Hermetic group, and the Hermetics are quite possibly the only organization that had a chance of beating the Technocracy to world control. They were experimenting with altering the consensus in isolated communities when the war started.<br /> <br /> All that said, I wouldn't assume the Hermetic World would end up like the modern world but with magic and more elitism. Nor would it be a small oligarchy of mages ruling over a world of peasants. In order to get the kind of worldwide paradigmatic change they would need to control everything they would have to incorporate their magic into everyone's lives. For that to happen they would have to foster the sense that anyone could potentially do magic.<br /> <br /> I see a world that is very hierarchical with ascension through the ranks being determined by proven application of Will. At the low end would be people who are largely unable to do magic, but who can use devices that are already set up for them. It doesn't leave these people out in the cold (again, you can't really build a consensual reality by leaving a huge chunk of people out of it) but it still isn't built for them. Instead, the world is built for the Mages, those who in theory serve everyone but in practice are largely above reproach. In the non fallen form they actually take their roles seriously, in the fallen form they are mostly paying lip service.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T13:15:23-07:00","id":1300053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299882-what-if-someone-else-won-the-ascension-war?p=1299986#post1299986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oooh.... tell me more.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Celestial Bureaucracy worked. To the point even if you &quot;looked like&quot; you were doing what hte concensus accepted.. you got paradox. Then the Opium wars happened.. and bam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T22:08:53-07:00","id":1300194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"http